<title>JAPAN: ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF SLALOM WINNER.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF SLALOM WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>SHIGA KOGEN, Japan 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a brief</p>
<p>profile of the winner of a mens World Cup slalom on Sunday:</p>
<p>Name: Thomas Stangassinger</p>
<p>Age: 31</p>
<p>Nationality: Austrian</p>
<p>World Cup wins: 5. All slaloms - Mount Sainte Anne (89),</p>
<p>Veysonnaz (93), Park City (93), Kitzbuehel (94), Shiga Kogen</p>
<p>(97)</p>
<p>Other feats: Slalom gold medallist at 1994 Lillehammer</p>
<p>Olympics. Placed second in four World Cup slaloms this season.</p>
</text>
